# Node.js UUID implementation: the platform's own `crypto.randomUUID`, reached as the host global as the browser's is.
# Term needs Node 22.3 or later (note/term/plan/term-load-install.md), and the global `crypto` is there from 19. It was
# `load <node:crypto>`, which put a Node import into every module that can raise an exception (the exception code is a
# UUID), so the browser compiler's bundle could not be built once a ported compiler module raised one (2026-10-04).
# Internal: reached only through the public uuid API.

dock load
  load <global:crypto>, name crypto

task generate-v4
  like text
  send back
    call crypto/random-uuid
